      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define and agree on packing, labeling and inventory procedures.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 323962,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Quick question on T4. For the pallets that have mixed parts for the metal line and some regular stock, how should we label them? I don't want to cause confusion.",
            "mentions": [
              542601
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Good question. I've created a draft Packing and Labeling Standards Guide in A2 to address this. The idea is to use color-coded labels: blue for general inventory, yellow for machine parts. For mixed pallets, we should use both labels. What does everyone think?",
            "mentions": [
              294961,
              323962,
              326777,
              534242
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 534242,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "The color coding is a good start. I'd suggest adding a large, clear destination zone code to the label format in A2. For example, 'ML-A' for Metal Line Area A. This will help movers who are just dropping and going, without needing to read the fine print. It prevents items from being staged in the wrong area.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 294961,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "So if a box has screws for the machine and also some other stuff, it gets two colors?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "That's a great addition. It makes the process much more robust. I'll update the label format in A2 to include a mandatory, large-font destination zone code. Let's make that the standard.",
            "mentions": [
              534242
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Correct. A yellow label for the machine parts, and a blue one for the general stock. And both would have the same destination code if they are going to the same general area.",
            "mentions": [
              294961
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 326777,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "The destination zone code is a good idea. It will help me quickly find all the parts I need for reassembly without having to search through general inventory pallets.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "Okay, sounds like we have a consensus. We will adopt the color-coding and large destination zone format as described in the updated A2. This is decision D3.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "Now, related to this is T5, the pre-move inventory count. We need to get a clean snapshot in A4 before we start moving boxes. To make that happen, all regular picking must stop before we count.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 534242,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "I suggest we set the cut-off for the inventory count at 4 PM on the Friday before each move weekend. That gives us a few hours to count and finalize the list in A4 before the move starts that evening.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 323962,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "4 PM works for me. That's enough time.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 294961,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "So no more touching stuff after 4?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "Exactly. All inventory in the move zone is frozen at 4 PM for the count. The proposal from @534242 makes sense. Any objections to setting 4 PM on the Friday of each move weekend as the cut-off time for completing the pre-move inventory in A4?",
            "mentions": [
              534242
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 534242,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "None from me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "Great. D4 is confirmed. I'll communicate this to the warehouse supervisor to ensure they halt operations in our zones accordingly. I'll take the lead on T5 and make sure the A4 sheet is ready before each weekend.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          }
        ],
