      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Clarify safety rules and hazard controls for heavy and dangerous goods.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 294961,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "I was looking at the inventory list and saw that batch of cleaning chemicals. The aisle to get them out is pretty narrow. I'm a bit concerned about moving those safely.",
            "mentions": [
              542601,
              534242
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "That's an important point to raise. Safety is our top priority. I've drafted the Safety and Hazard Checklist A3 for this exact reason, as part of T3. Please everyone take a look. It covers PPE, lifting, and handling of dangerous goods.",
            "mentions": [
              294961,
              323962,
              326777,
              534242
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 534242,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "The checklist in A3 is comprehensive. For the chemical move that @294961 mentioned, I strongly recommend we designate that a 'restricted access zone' during the lift. No one enters the area except the handler and a dedicated spotter. We should also do a trial run with an empty container to check clearances before moving the actual load.",
            "mentions": [
              294961
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 323962,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "The checklist looks ok. What kind of gloves do we need for the chemicals?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "The specific PPE requirements are linked in A3, but I'll make sure the correct chemical-resistant gloves are in the safety kit at the start of the shift. I'll also review this with the Health and Safety Officer today.",
            "mentions": [
              323962
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "I agree completely with the restricted zone and trial run. Let's make that a rule for any load marked as 'High Hazard'. This includes the chemical batch and the main body of the metal drawing machine. Are we all aligned on this approach?",
            "mentions": [
              534242
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 534242,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Yes, that's a solid plan. It minimizes risk significantly.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 294961,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "ok so I will need a spotter for that part. got it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Decision D6 is confirmed: the chemical load and the main machine body will require additional spotters and restricted access zones during the move. I'll mark this on the move plan.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 542601,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Now, back to the checklist A3 itself. I've incorporated the feedback and had it reviewed by the H&S Officer. Can we get a final approval from the team to make this the official checklist for the move?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 534242,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Approved. It's clear and covers the key risks.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
